 "30c5b79e9e238590162a8024f13a2b68d51e7f9716a809b4cadf712083c92a83" "basis" 590 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-x)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-4$ and $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/state.json" "file_sha256" "30c5b79e9e238590162a8024f13a2b68d51e7f9716a809b4cadf712083c92a83" "basis" 590 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "14ac6821779920b8bb5a0c599bd962881c8ed710e9269b01bc56512189f6eb3d" "basis" 590 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/state.json" "file_sha256" "30c5b79e9e238590162a8024f13a2b68d51e7f9716a809b4cadf712083c92a83" "basis" 590 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/state.json" "file_sha256" "30c5b79e9e238590162a8024f13a2b68d51e7f9716a809b4cadf712083c92a83" "basis" 590 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950745/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=8$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "455b098ef196edb68a19343572eda58785f9e1e403d78fcfb5f5d82d2cc9198a" "basis" 1040 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991810/state.json" "file_sha256" "455b098ef196edb68a19343572eda58785f9e1e403d78fcfb5f5d82d2cc9198a" "basis" 1040 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-cap