perbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}-{y}^{2}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-7998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}-{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}-{0}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ x & =\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are  $(\\pm 6,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-7998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-7998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-7998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\pm 1,0)"] ["math" "(\\pm 2,0)"] ["math" "(\\pm 3,0)"] ["math" "(\\pm 6,0)"] ["text" "$(-6,0)$ and $(1,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-7998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\pm 6,0)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9} & =0 \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x+2 & =0 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $(-2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-84035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/typ