quation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, there are no $y$-intercepts." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-84041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,-4)"] ["math" "(0,2)"] ["math" "(0,\\pm 2)"] ["math" "(0,\\pm 4)"] ["text" "There are no $y$-intercepts"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "There are no $y$-intercepts"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =-1,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,-1)$ and $(0,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-84044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db