 solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-(x-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-(0-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5}-4 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{5} & =5 \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =25 \\\\ y+5 & =\\pm 5 \\\\ y & =-10,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,-10)$ and $(0,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-84060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,0)"] ["math" "(0,\\pm 10)"] ["math" "(0,\\pm 2)"] ["text" "$(0,-10)$ and $(0,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,0)$ and $(0,10)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-84060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,-10)$ and $(0,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The hyperbola ${y}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15}=1$ intersects the line $y=-1$ at\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-1,$ we substitute $y=-1$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ (-1)^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $y=-1$  at $(0,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278389" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1$ intersects the line $x=-3$ at\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-3,$ we substitute $x=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $x=-3$ at $(-3,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-wor