$\nintersects the line $y=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-8008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=1,$ we substitute $y=1$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{(1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=1$ at the points $(\\pm 3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-8008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-8008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-8008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\pm 1,1)"] ["math" "(\\pm 2,1)"] ["math" "(\\pm 3,1)"] ["math" "(\\pm 6,1)"] ["text" "$(-6,1)$ and $(2,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-8008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\pm 3,1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-20{x}^{2}=180$ intersects the line $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=6,$ we substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-20{x}^{2} & =180 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-20(6)^{2} & =180 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-720 & =180 \\\\ {y}^{2}-80 & =20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =80+20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =100 \\\\ y & =\\pm 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=6$  at the points $(6,\\pm 10).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-10495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(6,\\pm 10)"] ["math" "(6,\\pm 15)"] ["math" "(6,\\pm 20)"] ["math" "(6,\\pm 25)"] ["math" "(6,\\pm 5)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(6,\\pm 10)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-170556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1$ intersects the line $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-170556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-1,$ we substitute $x=-1$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{27}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. \nSo, the hyperbola does not intersect the vertical line $x=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-170556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-170556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-170556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,\\pm 2)"] ["math" "(-1,\\pm 3)"] ["math" "(-1,\\pm \\frac{27}{4})"] ["math" "(-1,\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2})"] ["text" "There are no points of intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-170556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "There are no points of intersection"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1$ intersects the line $y=-x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-x)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-4$ and $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-278375" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acade