\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-10485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"] ["math" "x=\\pm 9"] ["text" "There are no points of intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-10485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "There are no points of intersection"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=8$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-277805" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=20$ intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\sqrt{5}x,$ we first replace $y$ with $\\sqrt{5}x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-\\sqrt{5}$ and $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278379" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-{y}^{2}=1$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{x}{4}$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=\\frac{x}{4},$ we first replace $y$ with $\\frac{x}{4}$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-4$ and $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7838443612f80e881d22e3fba6f19a79c53132ba3c1f35433f14d945b5365792"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "q-278380" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/state.json" "file_sha256" "c568ee07db6184bb18c03b3112315def5412995c423464fac58771effdde2ea8"} {"question" "e-5361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-5361.json" "file_sha256" "31e22435d9e7eaf94cca8b92ac67cdb4c2fb2126773677b75b3f033d5752185f"} {"question" "e-5361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{10} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-5361.json" "file_sha256" "31e22435d9e7eaf94cca8b92ac67cdb4c2fb2126773677b75b3f033d5752185f"} {"question" "e-7424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-7424.json" "file_sha256" "7b255932041fa02518390e63e38e96a4d548fb3294c799baa87a5d49792d1855"} {"question" "e-7424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2} & =28 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-7424.json" "file_sha256" "7b255932041fa02518390e63e38e96a4d548fb3294c799baa87a5d49792d1855"} {"question" "e-5362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the points where the hyperbola \n$\\dfrac{x^2}{10}-\\dfrac{y^2}{15}=1$\nintersects the line $y=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-5362.json" "file_sha256" "7b6bb7599d4b75c604dcb336e014789cea4198443c07fbb11a6493962702d3d8"} {"question" "e-5362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3,$ we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{9}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{3}{5} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6 & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-5362.json" "file_sha256" "7b6bb7599d4b75c604dcb336e014789cea4198443c07fbb11a6493962702d3d8"} {"question" "e-7425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/assets/c8d69cebc1c7388bb9bc8ac73152a9b2941156188917ee6b680f6758a3d777de.png)\n\nCalculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y = x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-7425.json" "file_sha256" "25cd3aaf0492e439b470be253e967dd451c434e0ea06ce6dfdd141259f4b302f"} {"question" "e-7425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{2}}{225} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{225}{16} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/example-7425.json" "file_sha256" "25cd3aaf0492e439b470be253e967dd451c434e0ea06ce6dfdd141259f4b302f"}] "usage" {"e-5362" [] "q-170556" [] "q-277802" [] "q-277805" [] "e-5361" [] "q-84041" [] "q-278375" [] "e-7425" [] "e-7424" []} "basis" 1333 "retractions" [[17592186088369 :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $((x - 2)^{2})/(5) - ((y + 4)^{2})/(16) = 1$."] [17592186087990 :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{x^{2}}{4} - \\frac{y^{2}}{9} = 1$ intersects the line $x =-1$."] [17592186087487 :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1$."] [17592186087487 :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) - \\frac{0^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) &= 1 \\\\\n(x + 1)^{2} &= 10 \\\\\nx + 1 &= ± \\sqrt{10} \\\\\nx &= -1 ± \\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\n\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right)\n$$"] [17592186087564 :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28$."] [17592186087564 :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7y^{2} - 5x^{2} &= 28 \\\\\n7y^{2} - 5(0)^{2} &= 28 \\\\\n7y^{2} &= 28 \\\\\ny^{2} &= 4 \\\\\ny &= ± 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2)$."] [17592186087488 :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola\n$\\dfrac{x^2}{10}-\\dfrac{y^2}{15}=1$\nintersects the line $y=-3$."] [17592186087488 :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3$, we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{y^{2}}{15} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - ((-3)^{2})/(15) &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{9}{15} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{3}{5} &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 6 &= 10 \\\\\nx^{2} &= 16 \\\\\nx &= ± 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3)$."] [17592186087565 :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y = x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/874/Source/Images/39c8aedbe6ab698c5a77db42509d3ef3.png)"] [17592186087565 :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x$, we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{x^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{16x^{2}}{225} &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} &= \\frac{225}{16} \\\\\nx &= ± \\frac{15}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186084952 17592186084953 17592186084954 17592186084955 17592186084956 17592186087145 17592186087146 17592186087147 17592186087148 17592186087149 17592186264737 17592186264739 17592186264741 17592186264743 17592186264782 17592186264783 17592186264785 17592186283902 17592186283904] "immutable_fields" [[17592186084951 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084951 :answer-field/id] [17592186084951 :answer-field/key] [17592186084951 :answer-field/type] [17592186087144 :answer-field/correct] [17592186087144 :answer-field/id] [17592186087144 :answer-field/key] [17592186087144 :answer-field/type] [17592186264736 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264736 :answer-field/id] [17592186264736 :answer-field/key] [17592186264736 :answer-field/type] [17592186264738 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264738 :answer-field/id] [17592186264738 :answer-field/key] [17592186264738 :answer-field/type] [17592186264740 :answer-field/correct] [17592186264740 :answer-field/id] [17592186264740 :answer-field/key] [17592186264740 :answer-field/type] [17592186264742 